
  As a Data Engineer,
  I want to mask the last 4 digits of the invoice_number column in the d_product_revenue_clone table
  So that sensitive customer invoice information is protected in compliance with data masking policies.

  Background:
    Given Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And Unity Catalog Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And I have access permissions to drop, create, and update tables in the schema
    And the source table "d_product_revenue" exists in schema "purgo_playground"
    And the "invoice_number" column is of datatype STRING and contains only numeric values of 10 digits

  Scenario: Drop the existing d_product_revenue_clone table if it exists
    Given table "d_product_revenue_clone" exists in schema "purgo_playground"
    When I execute the drop table statement for "d_product_revenue_clone"
    Then "d_product_revenue_clone" should not exist in schema "purgo_playground"

  Scenario: Create a replica of d_product_revenue as d_product_revenue_clone
    Given table "d_product_revenue_clone" does not exist in schema "purgo_playground"
    When I create "d_product_revenue_clone" as a replica of "d_product_revenue"
    Then "d_product_revenue_clone" must have the same schema and data as "d_product_revenue"

  Scenario Outline: Mask the last 4 digits of invoice_number with '*'
    Given d_product_revenue_clone contains an invoice_number with value "<original_invoice_number>"
    When I apply the masking PySpark logic to the invoice_number column
    Then the value of invoice_number becomes "<expected_masked_number>"

    Examples:
      | original_invoice_number | expected_masked_number |
      | 1234234534              | 123423****            |
      | 5555666677              | 555566****            |
      | 9876543210              | 987654****            |
      | 9999999999              | 999999****            |

  Scenario Outline: Handle invoice_number values shorter than 4 digits
    Given d_product_revenue_clone contains an invoice_number with value "<short_invoice_number>"
    When I apply the masking PySpark logic to the invoice_number column
    Then the value of invoice_number becomes "<expected_masked_short_number>"

    Examples:
      | short_invoice_number | expected_masked_short_number |
      | 123                 | ***                          |
      | 45                  | **                           |
      | 9                   | *                            |
      |                     |                              |

  Scenario Outline: Handle non-numeric or invalid format in invoice_number
    Given d_product_revenue_clone contains an invoice_number with value "<invalid_invoice_number>"
    When I apply the masking PySpark logic to the invoice_number column
    Then an error is raised with message "<expected_error_message>"

    Examples:
      | invalid_invoice_number | expected_error_message                                      |
      | 12A3456789            | Invalid invoice_number: non-numeric characters detected     |
      | 1234-56789            | Invalid invoice_number: special characters detected         |
      | NULL                  | Invalid invoice_number: value is null                      |

  Scenario: Validate the masking transformation for all rows in d_product_revenue_clone
    Given table "d_product_revenue_clone" contains N rows
    When I execute the masking logic on all rows
    Then all invoice_number values must have their last 4 characters masked with '*'
    And the total row count should remain N

  Scenario: Error when source table d_product_revenue does not exist
    Given table "d_product_revenue" does not exist in schema "purgo_playground"
    When I attempt to create a replica table
    Then an error message "Source table d_product_revenue not found in schema purgo_playground" is returned

  Scenario: Error when lacking permissions to drop or create tables
    Given I do not have DROP or CREATE permissions on schema "purgo_playground"
    When I attempt to drop or create a table
    Then an error message "Insufficient permissions to alter tables in schema purgo_playground" is returned